codex
The equality projection was truthful, but the backend retained a self-referential equality instead of substituting the constructor. I’m checking K’s native subsort-overloading mechanism so the list constructor itself can carry “all elements are strings” as a sort invariant. If it compiles to the same constructors used by the fixed semantics, this removes the predicate inversion entirely; I won’t keep it if it introduces a distinct runtime representation.
