codex
The compiled rule is sound for its stated context, but the bounded entry trace exposed a context mismatch: the real function continuation is the statement-list term `(Return(...) .Stmts):Stmts`, while the invariant and bridge used a bare `Return` statement. That explains why the bridge proved its standalone claim yet never matched the program. I’m repairing all three artifacts—the bridge-free theorem, bridge rule, and spec invariant—to the exact continuation emitted by the supplied statement-sequencing semantics, then re-proving the connection before reuse.
apply patch
